    <briefdescription>
<para>Drogon filter that screens requests for DoS/rate-limit violations before authentication. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>First element of both the INSECURE and SECURE chains. It builds a <ref refid="classDOSDetector_1a362a948824acc3cf457cb47e8d095cb5" kindref="member">DOSDetector::Request</ref> from the peer IP, method, path, hashed headers and body, and asks <ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1GateKeeper" kindref="compound">GateKeeper</ref> for a verdict. ALLOWED/WHITELISTED continue the chain; blacklist, rate limit, ban and internal error short-circuit with a corresponding HTTP status. The <ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1GateKeeper" kindref="compound">GateKeeper</ref> and <ref refid="classDOSDetector" kindref="compound">DOSDetector</ref> are shared service-locator objects held for the filter&apos;s lifetime. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Unknown verdicts fall through to continuing the chain (default branch). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
